{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/997062-any-good-stories-of-seer-chronicles","id":997062,"title":"Any good stories of Seer Chronicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T02:39:41-07:00","id":997062,"title":"Any good stories of Seer Chronicles?","content":"I must admit my guilty pleasure: the Seers of the Throne are my favorite Order. ^_^<br /> <br /> Despite how awesome the Diamond Orders are, how customizable the Free Council is, and how unique the Nameless Orders are, there is just something fascinating about these temporal power mad Mages. <br /> <br /> Due to their nature as default antagonists for 1st Edition though I've yet to hear any stories of Seer Chronicles. Are there any out there? If so, how was it? Were the Exarch's pleased with the game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-02-2016, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:47:45-07:00","id":997210,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Christian A&quot; had a Seer chronicle on planning stage. I could be wrong, though. He's the OP of many &quot;100 story hooks&quot; threads in the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:01:37-07:00","id":997293,"title":"","content":"I once ran a Seer story, but it was a Sleepwalker thing, not Awakened. It was an experimental solo game and the player didn't know they were working for the Seers but their character was a French soldier who was a part of Coalition forces in Afghanistan. Hit by an explosive, his face was scarred and he suffered hallucinatory visions in the desert that were the beginning of an Awakening that was interrupted. Returned to France after recovery in hospital, became a social outcast, and slowly went mad from recurring visions he ascribed to being brought on by pain meds. A recurring feature is an enormous, blazing eye, seeing every last piece of him with cold and absolute judgement.<br /> <br /> Until one day, while on a mundane walk, he is struck by a vision of absolute certainty that if he lets a man he sees in the crowd live, a child will suffer horribly. So he proceeds to try and beat the man to death in the middle of a crowded Paris street, fails (but still pretty seriously injures the guy), and is put on trial. Ends up confined to a sanitarium for treatment; the assault is blamed on mental trauma from the war and his injury.<br /> <br /> Fast forward about six months. He's off the pain meds. His visions are gone. He's feeling much better about himself. Until one day, he's walking through the halls and sees a painting of Justice on the wall; her blindfold is off and she is staring at him. When he looks away and looks back, the painting has reverted to normal but he's struck by the certainty that something is wrong. Later that day, he receives a visit from his sister - he does not have a sister - who is wearing a blindfold. She asks him some cryptic questions, tells him that he is being given a second chance to do his job, then leaves him the key to his cell and a promise that if he does what is asked of him, the rewards will be great.<br /> <br /> That night, he prays for some sort of sign from God - what he's come to see the flaming eye as - and receives a vision of the location of the man he assaulted long ago; the silhouette of the area painted in the stains the rain makes on the wall outside his cell.<br /> <br /> He escapes. Steals some rain gear and goes parkouring through the rooftops of Paris; assaults a man outside a night club to steal his clothes, then carries on to his target, police sirens dogging him all the way. He finds the guy's house. Finds the little girl of his visions hiding under her bed in terror. Slips through to the next room and puts a knife in the neck of the man he failed to kill long ago, right as police are charging up the steps.<br /> <br /> The man's cellphone rings. The assassin answers. He sees the woman whom he met earlier reflected in the spreading pool of blood. She asks him if he believes in miracles; if he has faith that God sees all and has a plan for the world. He answers that he does.<br /> <br /> &quot;Then reach into your coat pocket. Put on what you find there. Then walk outside.&quot;<br /> <br /> He reaches into his pocket. There is a heavy ring with a symbol of the rising sun upon it. He slips it on and, putting his faith in God, he opens the door and walks into a stairwell full of police officers. They all just run past him; like he's not even there. He walks outside in front of a barricade of police and they completely ignore him.<br /> <br /> A car is waiting.<br /> <br /> Ready to take him to his new home.<br /> <br /> And that's where it ended. Never got any further, but it was fun. I had plans to continue it but it didn't happen in a year, so...<br /> <br /> Fun part was, the player never even realized he was working for the Seers. He always assumed it was the Guardians or the Silver Ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:26:55-07:00","id":997402,"title":"","content":"Axelgear,<br /> <br /> That was an amazing story! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Highlights everything I love about the potential for storytelling in Seer Chronicles. Magnificently done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:29:31-07:00","id":997404,"title":"","content":"Zooroos, <br /> <br /> Thanks for the heads up. It would be interesting to hear from a ST planning a Seer Chronicle, and some of the points they feel is essential. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:46:10-07:00","id":997919,"title":"","content":"The plot of Killer7 is pretty hard to follow, but I've always thought of it as a Chronicle about the Praetorian (and possibly Hegemonic) Ministry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","name":"RdMarquis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}